---
/* What niwa is, in the words the site already publishes.
 *
 * One claim and one paragraph. The section makes no promise the
 * documentation does not keep, so it borrows nothing from anywhere else.
 */
---

<section class="why" id="why" aria-labelledby="why-title">
  <div>
    <h2 id="why-title">A setup you can read.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="why-body">
    <p>
      niwa is a configuration tool for macOS. One Luau script declares what the machine should
      be: packages, dotfiles, settings, and services. Applying it makes that true. Apply again
      and almost nothing happens, because almost everything is already true.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
